course: dictionary
lesson: 2121
title: Convert, one word many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them shows which one you need. «They converted the old barn into a house.» Here converted means changed into a different form or use.
explain: In maths, convert means to change a measurement into another unit. «Convert 3 metres into centimetres.» The unit changes, but the length stays the same. Say it as con-VERT when it is a verb.
explain: Convert can also be a noun, said CON-vert. A convert is a person who has changed their beliefs or opinion. «He'll be the most converted Toad that ever was» means he changed his mind completely. To check any meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Convert means to change something into a different form or use.
fact: In maths, to convert is to change a measurement or number into another unit, such as kilometres into metres.
fact: To convert money means to change it into another currency.
fact: A convert is a person who has changed their beliefs or opinion.
fact: In rugby, to convert a try means to kick the ball over the bar for extra points.
exercise: «They converted the old barn into a house.» What does converted mean here? | *Changed into a different form or use | Sold to a farmer | Knocked down completely | Painted bright red
exercise: To convert 2 kilometres into metres, how many metres are in each kilometre? | 1 million metres | 100 metres | *1000 metres | 10 metres
exercise: What is a convert? | *A person who has changed their beliefs or opinion | A tool for cutting wood | A large sum of money | A sort of rugby ball
test: «Mum will convert our spare coins into euros before the trip.» What does convert mean here? | Give the coins away | *Change money into another currency | Count the coins quickly | Put the coins in a bank account
test: In rugby, what does it mean to convert a try? | To stop the ball from going out | To run the ball over the line | To pass the ball to a teammate | *To kick the ball over the bar for extra points
exam: Jo says, «She is a convert now», meaning she has changed her opinion. What is a convert? | A person who sells things at a market | Someone who never changes their mind | *A person who has changed their beliefs or opinion | A type of measurement
